<includes>

    <include name="Hub_Slide_Group_OnWidgets">
        <animation effect="slide" time="400" end="0" start="0,$PARAM[posy]" tween="quadratic" easing="out" reversible="false" condition="$PARAM[condition]">Conditional</animation>
        <animation effect="slide" time="400" end="0,$PARAM[posy]" start="0" tween="quadratic" easing="out" reversible="false" condition="!$PARAM[condition]">Conditional</animation>
    </include>

    <!-- SKINMOD: Combine Widgets collision fix.
         "Combine Widgets" (use_as_widget) on a category makes its widgets selectable from the
         submenu button strip, grouplist 3002 (Hub_Submenu_Group). That strip is pinned at
         hub_submenuwidget_t (1300) inside Hub_Menu_Group, which carries the permanent -440
         offset described in section 1, so it rests at ~860px and is NOT affected by
         hub_widgets_shift_y. With the widget block pushed down 140px the first row lands on
         top of the strip.

         This slides widget wrapper group 340 back up by exactly hub_widgets_shift_y whenever
         the focused category has Combine Widgets enabled, so that category renders at the
         original upstream spacing. Because it translates the whole wrapper it cannot alter
         row-to-row pitch (same reasoning as section 3).

         The condition is character-for-character the strip's own visibility condition from
         shortcuts/generator/data/base/category_submenu.xml, so the two can never disagree.

         posy is applied when the condition is FALSE (see Hub_Slide_Group_OnWidgets above), so
         the condition is the *un*-combined case and the group rests at 0 (shift intact) there.

         time defaults to 1 (instant) so there is no window in which the row is mid-slide while
         the strip is fading in. Set it to 400 for a slide matching Hub_Slide_Group_OnWidgets. -->
    <include name="Hub_Slide_Widgets_OnCombined">
        <param name="posy">-hub_widgets_shift_y</param>
        <param name="condition">[String.IsEmpty(Container(300).ListItem.Property(use_as_widget))]</param>
        <param name="time">1</param>
        <definition>
            <animation effect="slide" time="$PARAM[time]" end="0" start="0,$PARAM[posy]" tween="quadratic" easing="out" reversible="false" condition="$PARAM[condition]">Conditional</animation>
            <animation effect="slide" time="$PARAM[time]" end="0,$PARAM[posy]" start="0" tween="quadratic" easing="out" reversible="false" condition="![$PARAM[condition]]">Conditional</animation>
        </definition>
    </include>



